+# Coupled run status
+
+Use the native command to inspect an existing run without provider calls, tool execution, API keys, or file mutation:
+
+```sh
+spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+`PATH` is resolved relative to the caller's current directory. The installed npm entry forwards the same command and arguments:
+
+```sh
+npx spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+`wire` requests count every durable ledger request. `task` requests count requests charged to the task budget; a missing native `charge` field uses the native task default. Failed and in-flight attempts count, and text logs are never used.
+
+For interrupted runs, an existing pending ledger contributes exactly once. If the pending directory, state directory, or ledger is absent, usage is unknown and the corresponding used and remaining totals are `null`, while limits remain known. Existing malformed data and symlinks on manifest or ledger paths are errors.
+
+The `completed` status is the recorded native completion state. It is not an independent verification result, qualification decision, or promotion authorization.
+
+The following is the completed synthetic example from `scripts.status_fixture.make`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "version": 1,
+  "status": "completed",
+  "stop_reason": "completed",
+  "iterations": [
+    {
+      "iteration": 1,
+      "task_id": "t1",
+      "termination": "completed",
+      "task_requests": 2,
+      "wire_requests": 3,
+      "changed_files": ["src/a.rs"],
+      "newly_verified": ["cargo test -q"]
+    }
+  ],
+  "pending": null,
+  "requests": {
+    "task_used": 2,
+    "wire_used": 3,
+    "task_limit": 192,
+    "wire_limit": 216,
+    "task_remaining": 190,
+    "wire_remaining": 213
+  }
+}
+```
